@page "/docs/images"
@layout Layout.DocsLayout

<PageTitle>Images · blux-ui</PageTitle>
<div class="pg-prose">
    <p class="pg-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
    <h1>Images</h1>
    <p class="pg-lead">Components that show a picture render a <code>BxImage</code>, and an image provider turns its source into resized, format-converted candidates for <code>srcset</code>.</p>

    <h2>BxImage</h2>
    <p><code>BxImage</code> renders one <code>img</code> with the <code>width</code>, <code>height</code>, <code>srcset</code>, <code>sizes</code> and <code>loading</code> a provider can fill in. <code>Alt</code> is required: pass an empty string for a decorative image. Without a provider (the default, <code>none</code>) the source is kept as it is and only <code>width</code>, <code>height</code> and <code>loading</code> are added, so nothing changes until you pick one.</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="Home.razor" Code="@BasicUsage" />
    <p>Supported parameters include <code>Width</code>, <code>Height</code>, <code>Sizes</code>, <code>Densities</code>, <code>Format</code>, <code>Quality</code>, <code>Fit</code>, <code>Modifiers</code> (provider specific), <code>Provider</code>, <code>Preset</code>, <code>Loading</code> (lazy by default, eager when preloading), <code>FetchPriority</code>, <code>Preload</code> and <code>Placeholder</code>.</p>

    <h2>Sizes and densities</h2>
    <p><code>Sizes</code> accepts space-separated entries: an unprefixed entry for the default and prefixed entries for the breakpoints of <code>o.Images.Screens</code> (Tailwind's: sm 640, md 768, lg 1024, xl 1280, 2xl 1536). Each entry applies from its breakpoint upward, and a value is a viewport percentage (<code>50vw</code>) or a width in pixels (<code>400px</code>).</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="@SizesUsage" />
    <p>For <code>"100vw sm:50vw md:400px"</code> with <code>"x1 x2"</code> the <code>sizes</code> attribute is <code>(max-width: 639px) 100vw, (max-width: 767px) 50vw, 400px</code> and the <code>srcset</code> holds the candidates 320w, 400w, 640w, 800w and 1280w: each size multiplied by each density. Without <code>Sizes</code>, <code>Width</code> and <code>Height</code> give an <code>x</code> descriptor per density (<code>1x</code>, <code>2x</code>). An unprefixed fluid size such as <code>100vw</code> is measured against the first breakpoint (or the widest screen) so it always produces realistic responsive candidates.</p>

    <h2>Providers</h2>
    <p>A provider is an <code>IBxImageProvider</code>: a name, whether it can resize, and <code>GetUrl(src, modifiers)</code>. Register it in <code>AddBluxUi</code>, on the server and in the WebAssembly client alike, and select it with <code>o.Images.DefaultProvider</code> or the <code>Provider</code> parameter. The settings become read-only once the first image is resolved.</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="Program.cs" Code="@ProviderUsage" />
    <p>The <code>Blux.UI.Images</code> package holds the providers of the main services, each built from the vendor's documentation:</p>
    <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-default" data-testid="image-providers">
        <table class="w-full min-w-xl text-start text-sm">
            <caption class="sr-only">Image providers</caption>
            <thead class="bg-muted text-highlighted">
                <tr><th scope="col" class="px-3 py-2 text-start">Registration</th><th scope="col" class="px-3 py-2 text-start">Service</th><th scope="col" class="px-3 py-2 text-start">URL</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var row in Providers)
                {
                    <tr class="border-t border-default">
                        <th scope="row" class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-mono text-xs font-medium text-highlighted">@row.Registration</th>
                        <td class="px-3 py-2 text-muted">@row.Service</td>
                        <td class="px-3 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted">@row.Url</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>A remote <code>src</code> is only sent to a provider that fetches remote images (Cloudflare, Netlify, Vercel, local) when its host is in <code>o.Images.Domains</code>; any other host is rendered untouched. <code>o.Images.Presets</code> names bundles of options (<code>Preset="thumb"</code>), and <code>AddTemplate</code> or <code>TemplateImageProvider</code> covers any service whose URLs follow a pattern.</p>

    <h2>Components that use it</h2>
    <p><code>BxAvatar</code> (and <code>BxColorModeAvatar</code>, <code>BxUser</code>), <code>BxColorModeImage</code>, <code>BxBlogPost</code>, <code>BxChangelogVersion</code>, <code>BxPageLogos</code> and the thumbnail of <code>BxChatAttachment</code> render a <code>BxImage</code>. Each takes an <code>ImageOptions</code> parameter forwarded directly to it. The avatar passes its size in pixels as the width and the height, so a provider serves a picture of exactly that size, and keeps its initials when the picture fails to load.</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="@ComponentUsage" />

    <h2>Preloading</h2>
    <p><code>Preload</code> loads the image eagerly with a high fetch priority and adds <code>&lt;link rel="preload" as="image" imagesrcset imagesizes&gt;</code> to the head through <code>HeadContent</code>. That needs a <code>HeadOutlet</code> in the app, which the Blazor Web App template has.</p>

    <h2>Resizing on your own server</h2>
    <p>The <code>Blux.UI.Images.Local</code> package is the counterpart of IPX: an endpoint that resizes and converts images with libvips (through NetVips) and a <code>local</code> provider that builds URLs to it. This site uses it, so the images of the <a href="/components/image">BxImage page</a> are real resized WebP files.</p>
    <CodeBlock Title="Program.cs" Code="@LocalSetup" />
    <p>In a WebAssembly client register only the URL builder, <code>o.Images.AddLocal(makeDefault: true)</code> from <code>Blux.UI.Images</code>, which has no server dependency. The endpoint is <code>_blux/img</code>, without a leading slash: the browser resolves it against <code>&lt;base href&gt;</code>, so an app served below a path base (<code>UsePathBase("/x")</code>, <code>&lt;base href="/x/"&gt;</code>) reaches its own optimizer at <code>/x/_blux/img</code> in every render mode. Call <code>UseRouting()</code> right after <code>UsePathBase</code>. An endpoint you give that starts with <code>/</code> is used literally, which is only right at the root.</p>

    <h3>Security</h3>
    <p>The endpoint is meant to face the internet, so every request is bounded in what it can reach and in what it costs.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Local sources are files below the web root (or the <code>FileProvider</code> you give), with image extensions only. Dot segments, backslashes, drive letters, protocol-relative paths and control characters are rejected with 400; hidden files are not served. <code>/img/a.png</code>, <code>/img//a.png</code> and <code>img/a.png</code> are one source with one cache budget.</li>
        <li>Remote images are fetched only from <code>AllowedRemoteHosts</code> (empty by default, 403 otherwise), on the default port of the scheme unless the entry names one (<code>images.example.com:8443</code>), with a size limit, a timeout, redirects only to the same scheme, host and port, no credentials in the URL, a content type check, and a refusal of loopback, private, link-local, carrier-grade NAT and other special-use addresses, including the IPv4 address inside NAT64, 6to4 and IPv4-compatible IPv6 forms. Fetches have their own limit and never hold a processing slot.</li>
        <li>Width and height are clamped (4096) and no output is larger than that whatever the ratio of the source or the <code>Fit</code>; a request without a size is scaled down to it. The quality is clamped to 1 to 100, and only <code>webp</code>, <code>avif</code>, <code>jpeg</code>, <code>png</code> and <code>gif</code> are produced. Widths are rounded up to a fixed list (the height follows) and qualities to multiples of 5, so a client cannot ask for every combination.</li>
        <li>Identical requests share one computation, processing is limited to <code>MaxConcurrency</code> images at a time with queued requests giving up with 503, and libvips is told to stop when no client waits for the result any more. Each client may start <code>RateLimitPermits</code> computations per <code>RateLimitWindow</code> (600 per minute by default, 429 with <code>Retry-After</code> beyond; cached variants are free). Clients are told apart by address: behind a reverse proxy call <code>UseForwardedHeaders</code> first, otherwise all your visitors share one allowance.</li>
        <li>An image keeps at most <code>MaxVariantsPerSource</code> variants: a new one replaces the least recently used instead of being refused, so junk requests cannot lock real variants out. The decode of a source is bounded in bytes and pixels.</li>
        <li>SVG is recognized by its root element, served as it is with a sandboxing <code>Content-Security-Policy</code>, and rasterized only when <code>RasterizeSvg</code> is on (off by default, because it runs an SVG renderer on the file) and a raster format is requested. libvips only loads JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF and GIF here, and the loaders it flags untrusted are blocked. Animated GIF and WebP files are served untouched.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Fit</h3>
    <p><code>Fit</code> follows sharp, which is what IPX uses. With a width and a height, <code>Cover</code> and <code>Outside</code> fill or cover the box and <code>Contain</code> and <code>Fill</code> produce exactly the box even from a smaller picture (<code>Contain</code> pads with transparency, or white for JPEG), while <code>Inside</code> never enlarges. With one side the ratio is kept and the picture is never enlarged. A <code>background</code> color for the padding is not configurable.</p>

    <h3>Caching</h3>
    <p>Variants are kept on disk in <code>CacheDirectory</code> (the temporary folder by default: choose a persistent one in production), limited to <code>MaxCacheBytes</code> counted in allocated disk blocks, the least recently used files going first (in the background, never in the way of a request). Responses carry an <code>ETag</code> and answer 304; the ETag of a remote image follows its content, and is only honored while the cached copy is within <code>RemoteCacheTtl</code>. With the <code>Version</code> option set, every URL carries it as <code>v</code> and is cached with <code>immutable</code> for a year: change it when your images change. Otherwise responses are cached for <code>CacheMaxAge</code> and revalidated.</p>
    <p>The native libvips binaries of <code>NetVips.Native</code> are LGPL licensed.</p>
</div>

@code {
    private sealed record ProviderRow(string Registration, string Service, string Url);

    private static readonly ProviderRow[] Providers =
    [
        new("AddCloudinary(cloudName)", "Cloudinary", "res.cloudinary.com/{cloud}/image/upload/c_fill,h_400,w_250/{path}"),
        new("AddImgix(domain)", "imgix", "{domain}/{path}?w=300&h=100&fit=crop"),
        new("AddImageKit(urlEndpoint)", "ImageKit", "{endpoint}/tr:w-300,h-300/{path}"),
        new("AddCloudflareImages(zone)", "Cloudflare Images", "/cdn-cgi/image/width=300,format=webp/{src}"),
        new("AddNetlify()", "Netlify Image CDN", "/.netlify/images?url=/owl.jpeg&fit=cover&w=50&h=50"),
        new("AddVercel(sizes)", "Vercel Image Optimization", "/_vercel/image?url={src}&w=1080&q=75"),
        new("AddBunny(baseUrl)", "Bunny Optimizer", "{zone}.b-cdn.net/{path}?width=500&quality=75&format=webp"),
        new("AddTemplate(name, template)", "Any service", "{src} {encodedSrc} {width} {height} {quality} {format}"),
        new("AddLocal(endpoint)", "Blux.UI.Images.Local", "_blux/img?src=%2Fimg%2Fa.png&w=384&f=webp"),
    ];

    private const string BasicUsage = """
        <BxImage Src="/img/team.jpg" Alt="The team on stage" Width="640" Height="360"
                 Format="webp" Quality="80" Sizes="100vw md:640px" />

        @* Decorative: an empty alt *@
        <BxImage Src="/img/texture.png" Alt="" />
        """;

    private const string SizesUsage = """
        <BxImage Src="/img/hero.jpg" Alt="Layered waves" Width="640" Height="360"
                 Sizes="100vw sm:50vw md:400px" Densities="x1 x2" Format="webp" />
        """;

    private const string ProviderUsage = """
        builder.Services.AddBluxUi(o =>
        {
            o.Images.Domains.Add("images.example.com");           // remote hosts a provider may process
            o.Images.AddCloudinary("my-cloud", makeDefault: true); // Blux.UI.Images
            o.Images.AddProvider(new MyProvider());                // your own IBxImageProvider
            o.Images.Presets["thumb"] = new BxImageOptions { Format = "webp", Quality = 60 };
        });
        """;

    private const string ComponentUsage = """
        <BxAvatar Src="/img/ada.jpg" Alt="Ada Lovelace" Size="BxSize.Lg"
                  ImageOptions="@(new BxImageOptions { Format = "webp", Quality = 80 })" />

        <BxBlogPost Title="Launch" Image="/img/cover.jpg" ImageAlt="The launch"
                    ImageOptions="@(new BxImageOptions { Sizes = "100vw md:50vw", Format = "webp" })" />
        """;

    private const string LocalSetup = """
        builder.Services.AddBluxImagesLocal(o =>
        {
            o.CacheDirectory = "/var/cache/my-app/images";
            o.Version = "2026-11-20";
            o.AllowedRemoteHosts.Add("images.example.com");
        });

        var app = builder.Build();
        app.MapBluxImages();   // GET /_blux/img?src=/img/team.jpg&w=640&f=webp
        """;
}
